arents=True, exist_ok=True)`) and writes the full task list as JSON synchronously.\n- **`backend/tests/conftest.py`** \u2014 sets `TASKS_DATA_FILE` to a fresh `tempfile.mkdtemp()` path before `app.main` is imported, so the module-level `store` singleton never touches the real data file. Comment explains the ordering constraint.\n- **`backend/tests/test_persistence.py`** (new) \u2014 7 tests covering restart survival, missing file, corrupt JSON, wrong top-level shape, wrong item shape, empty file, id-counter continuation after reload, and directory auto-creation. All pass.\n\n## How to verify\n```bash\ncd backend && python3 -m pytest -q   # 30 passed\n```\n\n## Known limitation / handoff item\nEverything is done except the one-line `.gitignore` change above, which needs to be applied by whoever has root-level write permission (or the sandbox's `allow` list extended to cover `Edit(./.gitignore)` / `Write(./.gitignore)`). Recommend the orchestrator apply it directly rather than looping back for another dev attempt, since it's a single line outside my scope's write access, not a code defect.", "meta": {"native_type": "result", "subtype": "success", "session_id": "634fabbc-ce46-4f8c-9558-b2651078472a", "is_error": false, "total_cost_usd": 0.47487929999999995}}
